assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 673 | 2026-10-26 | **Home groups as simple as possible (Build AG).** Built on row 672. Plan call 5, her answer: \"카테고리를 최대한 단순하게\". The Home's Touch and expression, Technique and Pieces doors now open straight onto one list of rooms, the way Rhythm already did (no topic level in between). Touch and expression: Dynamics, Touch (with the pedals and the ornaments, which were two small rooms), Tempo (with the four Home-only tempo games, was 'More about tempo'), Terms. Technique: Posture and hands, Hand positions (kp-fingers now only in Posture and hands), Playing scales, Fingerings in every key and chords. Pieces: Reading tunes, Signs and road maps, Form, Melody. Pitch keeps its seven topics (22 rooms would be too long for one list); Aural and Stories of music were already flat. No lesson, check or floor mark changed. HOME_DOOR (h-touch, h-tech, h-piece) are built from the old HOME_LIVE entries, which are then removed; HOME_OLD sends old links (concept=t-touch, t-tempo, k-posture, k-positions, k-play, c-reading, c-map) to the merged door with that room open. Also: the back button of a lesson or a question set opened from a door that skips its topic level now names the door (was 'Home' while it went back to the door), and the try tool under a list of rooms is numbered after the last lesson (the metronome showed '1'). Plan call 11 (sight-reading level), her question whether to build a generator here: no, decided to use the site's sight-reading generator (sightreading-generator/, its gradeParams.js already sets keys, metres, bars and hands per grade); drills keep the groundwork (Reading tunes room, 2-bar card). Recorded in the plan and both decision boards; nothing built for it. Tests: ag697.js (doors, rooms, old links, back labels, en/ko, no errors), full Home regression reg674 (every Home lesson and every room check, en/ko). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch697.py. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
